SUMMARY:CRH Seminar: FROM INHERITANCE TO INTERVENTION - Reprogramming the Sperm Epigenome
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Professor Sarah Kimmins\nDepartment of Pathology and Cell Biology\nUniversity of Montreal, Canada\n\nTitle: FROM INHERITANCE TO INTERVENTION: REPROGRAMMING THE SPERM EPIGENOME\n\nHost: Niamh Forde\n\nAbstract: Professor Kimmins' research centers on the molecular basis of epigenetic inheritance, with a particular emphasis on how the paternal environment shapes sperm epigenetic programming, early embryo development, and intergenerational disease risk.
